REGEDIT4

; A game site's session, on top of wine32-session.reg (a site builder
; applies it with reg-apply.py; not the dist's prefix: a console program
; would get an explorer it never asks for).
;
; - explorer.exe /desktop from RunServices: wineboot --init starts the
;   RunServices entries without waiting, before services.exe, so the
;   desktop process comes up beside the services instead of when the game
;   makes its first window and waits for it (win32u's get_desktop_window).
;   A program that starts explorer itself still does so: "explorer /desktop"
;   finds the desktop up and exits 0, as on demand. A 64-bit Wine game:
;   explorer at about 6-8 s instead of about 27 s, first window 32.4 s
;   mean against 34.6 s (7 runs each, 300 s timed).
;   winemenubuilder's entry stays.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\RunServices]
"desktop"="C:\\windows\\system32\\explorer.exe /desktop"
